Load shared mbstring in the multipart out-of-memory CGI test helper.

The helper starts CGI with -n and otherwise omits the shared extension loaded
by the parent test runner.  This leaves encoding conversion untested and
produces post=1 instead of the required memory-limit failure.  Keep all
memory-limit and expected-output assertions unchanged.

Will submit upstream.

--- a/tests/basic/oom_rfc1867.inc
+++ b/tests/basic/oom_rfc1867.inc
@@ -52,6 +52,15 @@
         '-d', 'fatal_error_backtraces=Off',
     ];
 
+    /* The CGI subprocess uses -n, so explicitly load shared mbstring when
+     * testing its multipart input conversion.  The parent test runner sets
+     * extension_dir to the modules from this build. */
+    $mbstring = ini_get('extension_dir') . '/mbstring.' . PHP_SHLIB_SUFFIX;
+    if (extension_loaded('mbstring') && is_file($mbstring)) {
+        $cmd[] = '-d';
+        $cmd[] = 'extension=' . $mbstring;
+    }
+
     foreach ($extraIni as $ini) {
         $cmd[] = '-d';
         $cmd[] = $ini;
